_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 8
---
order: 8
---
short_label: XI.8
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two straight lines are parallel, and one of them is at right angles to any plane, then the remaining one is also at right angles to the same plane.
----
proof:

Let {AB} and {CD} be two parallel straight lines, and let one of them, {AB}, be at right angles to the plane of reference.

I say that the remaining one, {CD}, is also at right angles to the same plane.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.8 diagram" src="propXI8.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (the same as XI.6's): the plane of reference P, the
    // parallels AB and CD, the shaded triangle BDE in the plane, with AD and
    // AE joined. DE is drawn in depth (E extends ZD by AM, half AB, in the
    // oblique view).
    //
    // BD and DE are solid slide twins over the triangle's edges, hidden at
    // rest (initiallyHidden) so they stroke from B and from D as joined and
    // drawn; the triangle BDE itself traces and fills when BE is joined.
    // Everything else added is transparent: PT, a faceless twin of P (the
    // filled plane would be raised over the figure if highlighted, #140);
    // BE, the triangle's third edge; and planeABDC, the plane through BD and
    // DA in which AB, BD and DC lie. The right angles (ABD, ABE by
    // XI.Def.3, BDE by construction, CDB, EDA, CDE as proved) are
    // angleMarkerRight squares, shown only on the slides that talk about
    // them so the four at D are not stacked at once.
    //
    // Joyce's "CD is at right angles to BC" means BD; BC is left literal.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): X, Y, Z (far-off direction
    // points), P0, A, C free; P1, P2, B sliders. All are givens, so none is
    // deferred. D, E, P3 are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["P","PT","P3","A","B","C","D","AB","CD"];
    var BDv   = GIVEN.concat(["BD"]);
    var PLN0  = BDv.concat(["planeABDC"]);
    var DEv   = BDv.concat(["E","DE"]);
    var ALL   = DEv.concat(["BDE","BE","AE","AD"]);
    var PLN   = ALL.concat(["planeABDC"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XI.8",
        elements: [
            "X;point;free;100000,100",
            "Y;point;free;100,-100000",
            "Z;point;free;50000,-100000",
            "P0;point;free;20,240;0;0,75,100",
            "P1;point;lineSlider;P0,X,190,240;0;30,75,100",
            "P2;point;lineSlider;P0,Z,50,110;0;30,75,100",
            "P3;point;intersection;P1,Z,P2,X;0;0",
            "P;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P3,P2;0;0;lightGray;brighter",
            "A;point;free;80,40",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A,Y,40,160",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "C;point;free;200,40",
            "D;point;intersection;B,X,C,Y",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "M;point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "E;point;extend;Z,D,A,M",
            "BDE;polygon;triangle;B,D,E;0;0;black;random",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E",
            // Slide twins, hidden at rest (see above).
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            "DE;line;connect;D,E",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "BE;line;connect;B,E;0;0;0",
            "PT;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P3,P2;0;0;0;0",
            "planeABDC;polygon;quadrilateral;A,C,D,B;0;0;0;0",
            "angABD;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,A,D",
            "angABE;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,A,E",
            "angCDB;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,C,B",
            "angCDE;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,C,E",
            "angBDE;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,B,E",
            "angEDA;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,E,A"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["BD","DE"],
        aliases: { "DB": "BD", "ED": "DE", "DA": "AD", "DC": "CD", "EB": "BE",
                   "ABD": "angABD", "DBA": "angABD",
                   "ABE": "angABE", "EBA": "angABE",
                   "CDB": "angCDB", "BDC": "angCDB",
                   "EDB": "angBDE",
                   "EDA": "angEDA", "ADE": "angEDA" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“If two straight lines are parallel, and one of them is at right angles to any plane,”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.8" }] },
            { text: "“then the remaining one is also at right angles to the same plane.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CD","PT"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} and {CD} be two parallel straight lines,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD"] },
            { text: "and let one of them, {AB}, be at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "I say that the remaining one, {CD}, is also at right angles to the same plane.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CD","PT"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} and {CD} meet the {plane of reference|PT} at the points {B} and {D}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["PT","B","D"] },
            { text: "Join {BD}.",
              visible: BDv,
              highlighted: ["BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then {AB}, {CD}, and {BD} lie in one plane.",
              visible: PLN0,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","BD","planeABDC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "planeABDC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "a line joining points on two parallels lies in their plane", ref: "XI.7" }] },
            { text: "Draw {DE} in the {plane of reference|PT} at right angles to {BD},",
              visible: DEv.concat(["angBDE"]),
              highlighted: ["DE","PT","BD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "DE",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "E",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angBDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "DE at right angles to BD", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "make {DE} equal to {AB},",
              visible: DEv,
              highlighted: ["DE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DE cut off equal to AB", ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "and join {BE}, {AE}, and {AD}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BE","AE","AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "BDE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "AE",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "AD",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Now, since {AB} is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"] },
            { text: "therefore {AB} is also at right angles to all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","PT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a line at right angles to a plane", ref: "XI.Def.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the angles {ABD} and {ABE} is right.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABD","angABE"]),
              highlighted: ["angABD","angABE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angABD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angABE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "And, since the straight line {BD} falls on the parallels {AB} and {CD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AB","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the angles {ABD} and {CDB} equals two right angles.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABD","angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["angABD","angCDB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angCDB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "interior angles on the same side", ref: "I.29" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {ABD} is right, therefore the angle {CDB} is also right.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABD","angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["angABD","angCDB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CD} is at right angles to BC.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["CD","angCDB"] },
            { text: "And since {AB} equals {DE}, and {BD} is common,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","DE","BD"] },
            { text: "the two sides {AB} and {BD} equal the two sides {ED} and {DB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BD","DE"] },
            { text: "and the angle {ABD} equals the angle {EDB}, for each is right,",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABD","angBDE"]),
              highlighted: ["angABD","angBDE"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {AD} equals the base {BE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","BE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "two sides and the included angle", ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "And since {AB} equals {DE}, and {BE} equals {AD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","DE","BE","AD"] },
            { text: "the two sides {AB} and {BE} equal the two sides {ED} and {DA} respectively,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BE","DE","AD"] },
            { text: "and {AE} is their common base,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {ABE} equals the angle {EDA}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABE","angEDA"]),
              highlighted: ["angABE","angEDA"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angEDA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "three sides equal", ref: "I.8" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {ABE} is right, therefore the angle {EDA} is also right.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angABE","angEDA"]),
              highlighted: ["angABE","angEDA"] },
            { text: "Therefore {ED} is at right angles to {AD}. But it is also at right angles to {DB}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angEDA","angBDE"]),
              highlighted: ["DE","AD","BD","angEDA","angBDE"] },
            { text: "Therefore {ED} is also at right angles to the plane through {BD} and {DA}.",
              visible: PLN.concat(["angEDA","angBDE"]),
              highlighted: ["DE","planeABDC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to two lines at their section", ref: "XI.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {ED} also makes right angles with all the straight lines which meet it",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["DE"] },
            { text: "and lie in the plane through {BD} and {DA}.",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["BD","AD","planeABDC"] },
            { text: "But {DC} lies in the plane through {BD} and {DA}",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["CD","planeABDC"] },
            { text: "inasmuch as {AB} and {BD} lie in the plane through {BD} and {DA},",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BD","planeABDC"] },
            { text: "and {DC} also lies in the plane in which {AB} and {BD} lie.",
              visible: PLN,
              highlighted: ["CD","AB","BD"] },
            { text: "Therefore {ED} is at right angles to {DC}, so that {CD} is also at right angles to {DE}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCDE"]),
              highlighted: ["DE","CD","angCDE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angCDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "But {CD} is also at right angles to {BD}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["CD","BD","angCDB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CD} is set up at right angles to the two straight lines {DE} and {DB}",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCDE","angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["CD","DE","BD"] },
            { text: "so that {CD} is also at right angles to the plane through {DE} and {DB}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCDE","angCDB"]),
              highlighted: ["CD","DE","BD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to two lines at their section", ref: "XI.4" }] },
            { text: "But the plane through {DE} and {DB} is the {plane of reference|PT},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DE","BD","PT"] },
            { text: "therefore {CD} is at right angles to the {plane of reference|PT}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","PT"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if two straight lines are parallel, and one of them is at right angles to any plane,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","PT"] },
            { text: "then the remaining one is also at right angles to the same plane.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","PT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.8") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.3":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.4":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI4/",
        "I.8":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI8/",
        "I.11":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "I.29":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI29/",
        "XI.Def.3": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI3/",
        "XI.4":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI4/",
        "XI.7":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI7/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let {AB} and {CD} meet the plane of reference at the points {B} and {D}. Join {BD}. Then {AB}, {CD}, and {BD} lie in one plane. [!just XI.7]

Draw {DE} in the plane of reference at right angles to {BD}, make {DE} equal to {AB}, and join {BE}, {AE}, and {AD} [!just I.11, I.3]

Now, since {AB} is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore {AB} is also at right angles to all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the plane of reference. Therefore each of the angles {ABD} and {ABE} is right. [!just XI.Def.3]

And, since the straight line {BD} falls on the parallels {AB} and {CD}, therefore the sum of the angles {ABD} and {CDB} equals two right angles. [!just I.29]

But the angle {ABD} is right, therefore the angle {CDB} is also right. Therefore {CD} is at right angles to *BC.*

And since {AB} equals {DE}, and {BD} is common, the two sides {AB} and {BD} equal the two sides {ED} and {DB}, and the angle {ABD} equals the angle {EDB}, for each is right, therefore the base {AD} equals the base {BE}. [!just I.4]

And since {AB} equals {DE}, and {BE} equals {AD}, the two sides {AB} and {BE} equal the two sides {ED} and {DA} respectively, and {AE} is their common base, therefore the angle {ABE} equals the angle {EDA}. [!just I.8]

But the angle {ABE} is right, therefore the angle {EDA} is also right. Therefore {ED} is at right angles to {AD}. But it is also at right angles to {DB}. Therefore {ED} is also at right angles to the plane through {BD} and {DA}. [!just XI.4]

Therefore {ED} also makes right angles with all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the plane through {BD} and {DA}. But {DC} lies in the plane through {BD} and {DA} inasmuch as {AB} and {BD} lie in the plane through {BD} and {DA}, and {DC} also lies in the plane in which {AB} and {BD} lie.

Therefore {ED} is at right angles to {DC}, so that {CD} is also at right angles to {DE}. But {CD} is also at right angles to {BD}. Therefore {CD} is set up at right angles to the two straight lines {DE} and {DB} so that {CD} is also at right angles to the plane through {DE} and {DB}. [!just XI.4]

But the plane through {DE} and {DB} is the plane of reference, therefore {CD} is at right angles to the plane of reference.

Therefore, *if two straight lines are parallel, and one of them is at right angles to any plane, then the remaining one is also at right angles to the same plane.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

This is a converse of proposition @XI.6.

This proposition is used in the proof of the next one as well as several others in this book.
